  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 152 AM CDT Sat Aug 29 2026\n\nSunday through Thursday\nAssessment...a certainty (>95%) of above normal temperatures.\n\nStarting Sunday the heat dome slowly builds north into the area. \nPrime time for the worst of the heat and humidity looks to be in the \nMonday through Wednesday time period. Based on progged temperatures \nand dew points, heat indices around or exceeding 100 are possible \nwith areas south of I-80 being favored. Record warm lows may be \nchallenged on some days. Refer to the climate section for more \nspecific information.\n\nHow warm it will get each day is dependent upon where the active \nstorm track is located. Two scenarios are in play and each has a 50% \nchance of occurring: 1) the storm track runs from Minnesota into \nWisconsin or 2) the storm track is over the area.\n\nRight now the model consensus has low (20-30%) rain chances on a \ndaily basis but favors areas north of I-80. This suggests that \nscenario 2 is the preferred scenario and suggests that any nocturnal \nincursion of convection may put a damper on daytime temperatures \nwith more clouds. If correct, heat indices would only get to around \n100.\n\nThursday night through Friday\nAssessment...low to medium (20-40%) confidence for rain with a late\nweek cool front.\n\nThe global models vary but suggest a possible cool front arriving \nlate in the week that may bring a brief respite from the heat and \nhumidity.\n\nThere are timing differences between the various models but the \nmodel consensus suggests late Thursday night into Friday as a \npossible frontal passage. The rain chances are only 20-30% \nindicating the forcing with the front is not overly strong.",
